## Deeper Pondering — So What?

The propagation failure is now four sessions deep. Every P0 fix has been "let the audit set the framing." That's useful maintenance, but it's triage of an architecture problem: the site was built sequentially (claims first, audits later), and fixing it page-by-page is a ratchet that will always lag.

The governing equation gap is the most interesting research observation today. If Option A is confirmed (tanh is a phenomenological compander with no governing equation), the central claim changes from "here is the coherence equation" to "here is a well-chosen compander with physical motivation for its parameters." That's still a useful effective description — Naka-Rushton, μ-law, Hill enzyme kinetics are all honest companders. But it changes the epistemic status of the "one equation describes reality" headline.

The wide binary ξ(ρ) gap is the most time-sensitive. If Gaia DR4 data lands before ξ(ρ) is published, TEST-02 joins TEST-04a in the post-hoc bin regardless of what the data shows. The explorer should treat this as urgent.
